## 🔌 Circuit Connections

The following connections are used to interface the Arduino UNO with the IR sensors, LCD display, and buzzer.

### 1. IR Sensors to Arduino UNO

| IR Sensor Pin     | Arduino UNO Pin |
| ----------------- | --------------- |
| First sensor VCC  | 5V              |
| First sensor GND  | GND             |
| First sensor OUT  | Digital Pin 2   |
| Second sensor VCC | 5V              |
| Second sensor GND | GND             |
| Second sensor OUT | Digital Pin 3   |

### 2. 16×2 LCD with I2C Module

| LCD I2C Pin | Arduino UNO Pin |
| ----------- | --------------- |
| VCC         | 5V              |
| GND         | GND             |
| SDA         | A4              |
| SCL         | A5              |

### 3. Buzzer to Arduino UNO

| Buzzer Pin   | Arduino UNO Pin |
| ------------ | --------------- |
| Positive (+) | Digital Pin 8   |
| Negative (−) | GND             |

### 4. Power Supply

* Connect the Arduino UNO to a computer using a USB cable.
* The USB connection supplies power to the Arduino and the circuit.
* Ensure all components share a common GND.

### ⚠️ Important Note

The pin numbers listed above are example connections. Make sure they match the pin assignments in your Arduino code and your actual circuit before uploading the program.
